WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.325
Quark keeps SKU attributes alongside the product record.
Open the SKU list.

2
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:13.646
Open a SKU, then switch to Attributes to review the values
attached to that item.

3
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:22.583
Start a new attribute entry. The lookup lists the
available attribute definitions for this record.

4
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:32.063
Choose the definition and enter its value. The attribute
stays in the context of the selected SKU.

5
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:42.795
Now follow that workspace into Quark's metadata tools.
Open SKU Management to inspect the form configuration.

6
00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:54.102
The SKU Attributes form is connected to the tabbed SKU
detail screen and to the attribute editing form.

7
00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:03.582
Create a draft from the selected module version. The
configuration work continues in that draft.

8
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:16.725
Return to the forms layer and locate SKU Attributes. Its
details provide a route into the form designer.

9
00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:29.221
Open the designer to inspect the attribute list layout.
The table and its properties appear in one workspace.

10
00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:41.124
Select a column to review its display settings. The
preview shows the form while the property panel exposes
the selected configuration.

11
00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:51.783
Adjust the displayed settings, then save the form
configuration. This recording shows editing in a draft,
not a production rollout.
